    "question": {
      ":question/id": "57882ea6-6fbd-5533-9db2-bd2bfe32da65",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 4 & -3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 4 & -3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 4 & -3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
